Version 0.4.1 (2026-02-04)
--------------------------
Performance Optimisations and Bounded Schema Cache (#45)

This is a **backward-compatible patch release** focused on significant performance improvements and bounded memory usage.

**Added:**
- `GetCacheStats() CacheStats` - Monitor cache performance (size, hits, misses, evictions, hit rate)
- `SetSchemaCacheConfig(maxSize int) error` - Configure cache size at runtime (default: 10,000 entries)
- `ClearSchemaCache()` - Manually invalidate cache when needed

**Performance Improvements:**
- Schema caching: repeated lookups served from a thread-safe in-memory cache (RLock on reads)
- Context shredding: 92% faster with 84% fewer allocations (14899ns → 1175ns)
- Event mapping: 71% faster with 50% fewer allocations (46027ns → 13402ns)
- JSON transformation: 59% faster (55024ns → 22816ns)
- String operations: 55% faster with strings.Builder (201ns → 91ns)
- Schema extraction: 89% faster with 98% fewer allocations (6253ns → 701ns)

**Technical Details:**
- Thread-safe bounded cache: shared read lock on hits, exclusive lock only on writes
- Nuke eviction strategy: cache is cleared when full (default size of 10,000 makes this rare)
- Pre-allocated maps and slices with capacity hints reduce allocations
- Zero race conditions verified

**Migration:** Fully backward compatible - no code changes required. Cache configuration is optional.

